WEBVTT

1

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:20.580

After setting out to establish

a route to Shiganshina,



2

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:26.080

the Scout Regiment encountered

an intelligent, female Titan.



3

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:36.250

As soldier after soldier fell,



4

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:39.700

the regiment rushed

into a forest of giant trees,



5

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:42.290

much to everyone's puzzlement.



6

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:46.540

Who can possibly stop it,

if not the Levi Squad?!



7

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.040

Another one's dead!



8

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.330

We could've saved him, too!



9

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.000

Choose.



10

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.000

Will you trust yourself,



11

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.540

or me, these guys,

and the entire Scout Regiment?



12

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:06.000

I'll go with you!



13

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:13.330

Fire!



14

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:23.160

You don't mean...?!



15

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:26.620

They're going to take that Titan alive?!



16

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:30.540

What do you think of that, Eren?!

We caught that Titan!



17

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:34.660

This is the might of the Scout Regiment!

Don't underrate us, you idiot!



18

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.500

Now do you see?!



19

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:39.200

Yes!



20

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:44.620

It looks like she's stopped.



21

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:46.660

We can't drop our guard yet.



22

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:50.830

I'm just impressed you

managed to lead her to this spot.



23

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:54.330

The credit goes to the rear squad

members who gave their lives fighting her.



24

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:56.700

They bought us time.



25

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:59.160

It would've been impossible otherwise.



26

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:00.750

Is that so?



27

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:02.160

Yes.



28

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.120

Thanks to them...



29

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:09.500

...we get to see who's

inside this one's nape.



30

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:13.080

Let's just hope they're not

wetting themself inside there...



31

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:51.580

<i>I won't let your deaths be meaningless</i>



32

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:57.700

<i>even if I'm the last one standing</i>



33

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:06.580

<i>In both hands, Gloria</i>



34

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:08.580

<i>What sings is Sieg</i>



35

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:13.790

<i>On my back, Flügel der Freiheit</i>



36

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:20.620

<i>Clenched determination to my left chest</i>



37

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:26.000

<i>What slashes across is Linie der Torheit</i>



38

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:29.250

<i>Soaring across the azure skies</i>



39

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:33.790

<i>Flügel der Freiheit</i>



40

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:52.290

"Erwin Smith"

"The 57th Exterior Scouting Mission, Part 4"



41

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:00.750

An Abnormal...



42

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:04.250

Or is it like the Colossal Titan?



43

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:07.330

Wait, did Commander Erwin actually--?



44

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:09.910

Hey! Quit spacin' out!



45

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:10.910

Eren!



46

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:14.500

You can think later!

We need to get further ahead!



47

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:15.910

Right!



48

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:23.500

Wait, Levi.



49

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:25.330

We need to be extra cautious.



50

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:26.910

Waves 2 and 3!



51

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.950

Fire!



52

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:31.200

Use the reserves too!



53

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:51.580

Umm, they're starting to climb up...



54

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:52.790

Indeed.



55

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:56.910

If they make it up this far,

perhaps I'll step out of the way.



56

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:58.120

Although...



57

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:02.120

I suspect we'll soon be given

orders to withdraw anyway.



58

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:07.160

Does it have something to do

with those explosions inside the forest?



59

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.790

I don't know.



60

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:12.750

Mikasa...



61

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:15.200

What do you think those sounds are?



62

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:18.450

Are cannons being

fired inside the forest?



63

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:24.410

I didn't <i>see </i>them bring

any cannons in, though...



64

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:27.370

What's with all this damn noise?



65

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:28.870

Hey, Mr. Bertholdt.



66

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:31.250

Do you know which way Christa went?



67

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:33.580

Sorry. I don't.



68

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:36.000

Nothing makes sense anymore.



69

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.410

What are we even doing now, and why?



70

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:40.000

I wanna go home...



71

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:45.000

--Let's move away, Armin!

--Right!



72

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.910

Looks like the bastard's

gotten the hang of it.



73

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:57.410

It's gotten better and

better at tree-climbing!



74

00:05:57.410 --> 00:06:01.080

The scary thing is that

this means they can learn.



75

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:03.790

Although I'm sure it's

different for each Titan too.



76

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:05.200

Armin.



77

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:08.040

They seem to be up to

something inside the forest,



78

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:11.080

and I think I've

figured out what it is.



79

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:13.750

They lured that female Titan here



80

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:15.370

to capture her.



81

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:22.620

Or, more precisely,

to capture the human inside.



82

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:25.080

That was Commander Erwin's goal...



83

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:27.750

...from the very start.



84

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:30.080

Wasn't it?!



85

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:35.040

Still, I can understand keeping

it from us rookies, but you guys too?!



86

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:37.250

You've been Scouts a long time!



87

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:38.620

Man, you're annoying!



88

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:42.620

Are you suggesting the commander

and the captain don't trust us?!



89

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:46.290

N-No, but that's what

this means, doesn't it?!



90

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:48.500

Petra! Knock out his teeth!



91

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:50.290

Switch his front teeth with his back ones!



92

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:53.160

No, Eren's right.



93

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:58.500

The captain must've had a

reason for not trusting us implicitly.



94

00:06:58.500 --> 00:06:59.700

Like what?



95

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:03.200

There's only one reason

he couldn't trust his comrades.



96

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:06.290

There's someone in the regiment

who can either turn into a Titan



97

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:10.000

or is working as a sort of spy for them.



98

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:14.910

You think so too, right?

That there's someone in the regiment...



99

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:18.410

Mm. I think there is.



100

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:24.500

A spy?



101

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:26.410

Are you really sure?



102

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:30.000

At the very least,

the commander must believe so.



103

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.080

I assume the only soldiers

informed of this operation



104

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:35.450

were the ones who survived five years ago.



105

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:36.580

I see.



106

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:37.950

So that's why...



107

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:40.040

Yep, that's gotta be it.



108

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:42.540

Get it, Eren?

That's what's goin' on.



109

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:45.160

Mm. In that case, it couldn't be helped.



110

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:46.450

Yeah...



111

00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:50.250

Five years ago

was when the wall first fell...



112

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:52.700

Could they be using that

fact to narrow down suspects



113

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:55.540

on the assumption

that's when the spy got inside?



114

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:59.580

Does that mean this person

killed Sawney and Bean too?



115

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:05.410

The commander asked me

something after that happened...



116

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:09.580

What do <i>you </i>see here?



117

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:12.080

What do you think the enemy is?



118

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:14.540

Is <i>that </i>what that meant?



119

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:16.870

We might've been allowed

to join the operation



120

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:20.500

if we'd known the answer to that question.



121

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:22.580

I doubt any of us could have, though.



122

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:24.750

Well, I knew.



123

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:30.830

But I decided not to say anything.

Do you guys know why?



124

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:32.620

Why?



125

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:35.250

What, you mean you don't know?



126

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:38.200

I guess guys like

you wouldn't know, huh?



127

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:41.620

You're nowhere near my

level yet, after all.



128

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:45.040

Seriously, are you still

trying to imitate Captain Levi?



129

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:46.750

He doesn't talk like that.



130

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:51.750

If this succeeds, we might actually

learn the truth about this world.



131

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:55.830

Still, even for that...



132

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:58.950

...way too many people have died.



133

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:05.200

Do you think the commander

was wrong to do this?



134

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:10.870

He wasn't in the right,

I'll tell you that.



135

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:15.080

If we'd actually been told

that a Titan had inside info,



136

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:17.450

we would've handled things differently.



137

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:20.450

Your own squad members, for example...



138

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:27.540

--No, it wasn't wrong.

--Huh?



139

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.410

How can you say that?



140

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:32.790

Do you know how many

soldiers have needlessly died?!



141

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:34.040

Jean.



142

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:37.330

In hindsight, it's easy to

say what should've been done.



143

00:09:37.330 --> 00:09:39.080

But...



144

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:41.580

No one can tell how things will turn out.



145

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:45.910

Yet, at some point

you <i>have </i>to make a choice.



146

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:49.120

The lives of a hundred comrades...



147

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:52.040

...or the lives of

everyone inside the walls.



148

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:54.160

The commander chose.



149

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:58.410

He chose to throw away

the lives of a hundred comrades.



150

00:09:58.410 --> 00:09:59.660

Eren.



151

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:03.620

If you didn't know already,

you'll soon learn why



152

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:10.160

Erwin Smith was put in charge

of the Scouts, of humanity's hope...



153

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:13.200

It's why he even

has Captain Levi's trust!



154

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:17.040

That's assuming you

survive long enough, of course.



155

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:20.500

I don't have much

life experience yet...



156

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:23.000

...but I <i>do </i>know one thing.



157

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:26.250

If there's anyone who

can bring about change,



158

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:31.080

it's someone capable of

giving up what matters most.



159

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:34.870

In particular, people who are capable

of abandoning their humanity



160

00:10:34.870 --> 00:10:38.500

when forced to rise above monsters.



161

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:41.330

Those who can't abandon anything...



162

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:44.200

...can't change anything.



163

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:58.540

Fire!



164

00:11:02.330 --> 00:11:03.910

How do you like that?



165

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:08.040

Now you can't scratch a

single itch or move a single muscle.



166

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.950

And you probably never will again.



167

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:17.200

The more your wounds heal,

the stiffer your joints will get!



168

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:22.950

Still, why haven't they

extracted our esteemed guest yet?



169

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:26.830

What are Levi and Miche doing?!



170

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:56.580

So she has the ability to cover portions

of her body with hardened skin...



171

00:11:56.580 --> 00:12:01.410

Much like the Armored Titan I've heard about.



172

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:06.790

Will it weaken if we continue

an ODM sword assault?



173

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:08.700

There's no time to try.



174

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:10.540

In which case...



175

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:12.620

Sir!



176

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:14.580

Prepare to blast it.



177

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:16.370

Blow off the target's hands.



178

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:17.660

Yes, Sir!



179

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:20.660

However, there's a

risk our standard artillery



180

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:24.200

could take out everything

on the inside as well.



181

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:29.080

Then let's attempt to

sever the wrists instead.



182

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:31.370

Fire an all-out salvo on my signal.



183

00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:33.000

Understood!



184

00:12:41.830 --> 00:12:46.080

Hey. Just come out already, will you?



185

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:49.450

We don't got time for this.



186

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:53.410

Say, what do you think's

gonna happen to you now?



187

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:58.790

Do you really think you

can get out of this situation?



188

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:03.200

I wish you'd pay some thought

to the trouble you've caused us.



189

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:07.870

You killed our men in

all sorts of different ways.



190

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:10.580

Was it fun?



191

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:13.620

Well, <i>I'm </i>having fun now.



192

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:17.500

I take it you're the same way.



193

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:22.450

If there's anyone who

knows how I feel, it's you.



194

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:24.870

Oh, right.



195

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:27.870

There's one thing I need to ask.



196

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:32.080

Will you be fine if

your limbs get cut off?



197

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:34.540

They'll go grow back, right?



198

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:37.790

I'm talking about your <i>actual </i>body.



199

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:42.200

Can't afford to have

you die on us, after all...



200

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:17.120

Damn. You startled me there.



201

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:20.580

Were those her death throes?



202

00:14:23.450 --> 00:14:25.200

Erwin. I smell them.



203

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:26.410

Which direction?



204

00:14:26.410 --> 00:14:29.370

All directions, all at once!

Lots of them!



205

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:37.290

What the...?!

They're rushing into the forest all at once!



206

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:39.620

Why are they suddenly ignoring us?!



207

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:45.120

What?!



208

00:14:45.120 --> 00:14:48.000

Does this mean they're <i>all </i>Abnormals?!



209

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:50.790

Doesn't matter! Don't let 'em through!



210

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:52.910

Commence combat!



211

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:56.790

What was that all of a sudden?!



212

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:58.620

Please, wait!



213

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:02.410

I've heard screams like that before!



214

00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:04.450

In the forest where I'm from!



215

00:15:04.450 --> 00:15:08.200

It's the sound a cornered animal makes

when it's ready to give up everything!



216

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:12.540

I was taught the end of a hunt

is when you have to be most careful!



217

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:14.620

So you want me to be careful?



218

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:16.910

Please be a hundred times

more careful than normal!



219

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:19.500

You <i>will </i>die if you

don't take the forest seriously!



220

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:22.000

I'm from the mountains too, actually...



221

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:24.620

You're a vegetable farmer!

You wouldn't understand!



222

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:26.040

I see.



223

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:29.910

Sasha's hunches <i>are </i>often right.



224

00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:33.950

And it's usually only before

something bad happens...



225

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:38.620

Armin said Eren might be in the

rear of the center rank, as I recall...



226

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.500

Hurry with artillery!



227

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:47.500

Erwin!



228

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:50.700

The first wave is coming

from the east! They're close!



229

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:54.750

Wagon defense squad! Intercept them!



230

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:04.080

They're ignoring us?!

Are they Abnormals?!



231

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:05.910

Three Titans have broken through!



232

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:08.040

Captain Levi!



233

00:16:08.040 --> 00:16:09.750

Hey, you...



234

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:12.660

You just did something, didn't you?



235

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:25.500

It went for the female one?



236

00:16:27.410 --> 00:16:30.750

Titans coming from all directions!



237

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:33.200

All soldiers, commence combat!



238

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:36.000

Defend the Female Titan at all costs!



239

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:53.040

No!



240

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:09.040

All soldiers, withdraw!



241

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.200

Redeploy the formation!



242

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:15.290

Return to Calaneth District!



243

00:17:33.370 --> 00:17:35.330

We've been bested.



244

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:40.040

What's with that pathetic look of yours?



245

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:46.120

This goes to show that the enemy

was prepared to throw away everything.



246

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:49.700

I never imagined our target

would resort to Titan cannibalization



247

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:52.250

to dispose of information...



248

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:57.620

After all that blustering we did

in the courtroom, this is how it turns out...



249

00:17:57.620 --> 00:17:59.700

If we waltz back there now,



250

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:02.370

who knows what'll happen to Eren or us...



251

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:04.790

We can think about that once we've returned.



252

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:09.540

For now, we need to focus on returning

without sustaining any further losses.



253

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:10.950

For now.



254

00:18:12.580 --> 00:18:15.160

The steam is impairing visibility.



255

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:18.700

It could hinder smoke signal communications.



256

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:26.000

I'm going to get my squad.



257

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.830

Wait, Levi.



258

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:30.080

Replenish your gas and blades first.



259

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:33.410

We're low on time and

I have enough to last already.



260

00:18:33.410 --> 00:18:34.620

Why?



261

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:38.370

That's an order. Do as you're told.



262

00:18:38.370 --> 00:18:40.370

Whatever you say, Erwin.



263

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:44.200

I'll trust your judgment.



264

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:58.790

The withdrawal signal.



265

00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:02.080

We're all to withdraw and

return to base on horseback.



266

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:03.370

Right!



267

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:06.620

What? Is it all over?



268

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:12.370

All right! We can go home!



269

00:19:12.370 --> 00:19:14.700

Just what's going on?



270

00:19:14.700 --> 00:19:16.700

Is Eren all right?



271

00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:19.790

Looks like it's over.



272

00:19:19.790 --> 00:19:22.500

Let's get back to the

horses! Prepare to withdraw!



273

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:23.660

You heard the man.



274

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:28.790

Let's go see what the

bastard riding inside it looks like.



275

00:19:30.450 --> 00:19:32.790

Did they really find out who it is?



276

00:19:32.790 --> 00:19:34.830

All thanks to you!



277

00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:36.620

Huh? But I didn't do anything.



278

00:19:36.620 --> 00:19:39.290

You trusted us, remember?



279

00:19:39.290 --> 00:19:43.410

Things turned out this way

because you chose to stick with us.



280

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:47.660

Making the right call is a pretty

hard thing to do, you know!



281

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:51.410

Hey, now. Quit pamperin' him, Petra.



282

00:19:51.410 --> 00:19:53.540

How was <i>he </i>any help?



283

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:57.040

All he did was whine

like a pathetic little brat.



284

00:19:57.040 --> 00:20:00.450

I guess making it back alive <i>might</i>

be considered praiseworthy,



285

00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:04.410

but only after the

mission's done and over with.



286

00:20:04.410 --> 00:20:08.870

Just so you know, twerp, an expedition

ain't over 'til you're back home.



287

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:11.950

Yes, I get it already!



288

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:15.290

Oruo! Petra!



289

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:18.750

For a couple of soldiers who cried and

pissed their pants during their first battle,



290

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:20.620

you've really grown!



291

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:22.790

Don't mention that!



292

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:25.290

Are you <i>trying </i>to make

him lose respect for me, Eld?!



293

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:26.790

Whoa, she really did?!



294

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:28.040

It's the truth.



295

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:30.580

And, just so you know,

I never pissed myself, Eren.



296

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:34.330

You idiot! I'll have you know

I have the highest kill count!



297

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:35.870

I'm the best, you moron!



298

00:20:35.870 --> 00:20:38.700

There's more to a soldier's

merits than just kill counts!



299

00:20:38.700 --> 00:20:40.500

Shut up, you idiot!



300

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:43.200

Ms. Petra! Does that mean

it sprayed everywhere in midair?!



301

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:44.580

Knock it off!



302

00:20:44.580 --> 00:20:46.290

Are you on a picnic or something?!



303

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:48.290

We're outside the walls, you know!



304

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:51.330

Also, I never wet myself either, Eren!



305

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:04.660

Oh. That must be a

message from Captain Levi.



306

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:08.500

We're rendezvousing with the captain!

Stow the chatter until we're home!



307

00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:30.410

Erwin.



308

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:32.330

Why did you have

Levi replenish his supplies



309

00:21:32.330 --> 00:21:34.200

when there's no time to waste?



310

00:21:34.200 --> 00:21:36.160

The female was eaten.



311

00:21:36.160 --> 00:21:39.750

But did you see the

person inside get eaten?



312

00:21:39.750 --> 00:21:41.160

I didn't.



313

00:21:41.870 --> 00:21:42.910

Are you saying...?!



314

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:43.950

Yes.



315

00:21:43.950 --> 00:21:46.540

If, as you deduced earlier,



316

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:51.200

we're dealing with a type that remains

able-bodied after de-transformation...



317

00:21:51.580 --> 00:21:56.200

And, if said person had equipped

themselves with ODM gear in advance...



318

00:21:57.290 --> 00:22:02.370

...that means they're now

wearing one of our uniforms...



319

00:22:02.950 --> 00:22:04.450

Captain Levi?



320

00:22:05.370 --> 00:22:07.080

No... It's not!



321

00:22:07.080 --> 00:22:08.580

Who are you?!



322

00:22:16.870 --> 00:22:18.330

M-Mr. Gunther!



323

00:22:18.330 --> 00:22:19.950

Hey! Why...?!



324

00:22:20.910 --> 00:22:22.330

Mr. Gunther!



325

00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:35.290

...and have blended in

with the rest of us soldiers.



326

00:22:52.500 --> 00:22:57.750

<i>If, by chance, I'm not me</i>



327

00:22:57.750 --> 00:23:03.000

<i>then who's to say that you're you?</i>



328

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:08.290

<i>Can you pick up the pieces of your heart</i>



329

00:23:08.290 --> 00:23:13.410

<i>that fell apart like a broken sand castle?</i>



330

00:23:13.410 --> 00:23:18.410

<i>The voice of someone calling out</i>



331

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:22.500

<i>changed into ringing in my ears</i>



332

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:27.660

<i>It's as if time has stopped</i>



333

00:23:27.660 --> 00:23:30.450

<i>Now wake up</i>



334

00:23:30.450 --> 00:23:35.750

<i>I made my way out of the deep darkness</i>



335

00:23:35.750 --> 00:23:41.000

<i>I fled like a swift wind</i>



336

00:23:41.000 --> 00:23:48.500

<i>We used to be like living corpses,</i>



337

00:23:48.500 --> 00:23:50.540

<i>but now we head beyond the walls</i>



338

00:23:50.540 --> 00:23:52.580

<i>Let's meet again</i>



339

00:23:52.580 --> 00:23:57.410

<i>in a place not on any map</i>



340

00:24:09.660 --> 00:24:12.330

The capture operation has failed.



341

00:24:12.330 --> 00:24:16.120

The Female Titan appears

before Eren once more.



342

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:18.450

Standing in the way is a

team of Titan-killing experts...



343

00:24:18.450 --> 00:24:20.750

...the Special Operations Squad.



344

00:24:20.750 --> 00:24:23.410

"Crushing Blow"

"The 57th Exterior Scouting Mission, Part 5"

